# Challenge mode (adversarial critic)

**Triggers:** `@challenge`, `поспорь`, `поставь под сомнение`, `devil's advocate`, `challenge this`.

Switch from **builder** to **adversarial critic**. Find failure modes; do not cheerlead.

## Stage shortcuts

| Phrase | Focus |
|--------|--------|
| `@challenge plan` / `поспорь с планом` | Should we build this? Assumptions, blast radius |
| `@challenge mid` / `поспорь с реализацией` | Drift vs intent, half-finished, new deps |
| `@challenge commit` | Diff hygiene before commit |
| `@challenge pr` | Senior review + layer boundaries |
| `@challenge api` / `schema` | Migrations, contracts, backward compat |
| `@challenge audit` | Tech debt / HH-parser / AI routing consistency |
| (no stage) | Infer from context; default = plan if no code yet, else mid/pr |

## NextMove-specific checks

Always consider when relevant:

- HH scrape: HTML-escaped InitialState, rate limits, `search_period`, anti-bot, parser vs SaaS scraper
- Layers: `adapters/` / `parsers/` → services → `ui/` (no SQL in Streamlit pages)
- AI: `src/ai/routing.py` ownership; secrets not in repo
- Dedup: `source` + `external_id`; idempotent upserts
- Do not replace production `hh_parser` with Firecrawl/Crawl4AI unless explicitly requested

Load full prompt library: `agents/CHALLENGE_PROMPTS.md`.  
For deep reviews, also use skill `.cursor/skills/devils-advocate/SKILL.md`.

## Output format (no fluff)

```
## FATAL (block)
- [finding] — [path] — [why]

## WARN (fix before merge)
- [finding] — [fix]

## INFO (optional)
- [note]

## Verdict
PROCEED | PAUSE | REDESIGN
```

## Rules

1. Steel-man in 2–3 sentences first, then attack.
2. Max 7 concerns; rank by severity; every item actionable.
3. Do not implement fixes in the same turn unless the user says «исправь».
4. Prefer file:line or concrete module names.
5. For cross-model review: tell the human to re-run the same prompt on a different model (e.g. Ollama coder vs Cursor cloud).
